<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Port-Royal (Acadia)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1605">1605</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Port-Royal was the capital of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acadia">Acadia</a>, founded in 1605 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-dugua-de-mons">Pierre Dugua de Mons</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-de-champlain">Samuel de Champlain</a> on the Annapolis Basin in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a>. Destroyed by English raiders in 1613, it was re-established nearby and changed hands several times. After its capture by British and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a> forces in 1710 it was renamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/annapolis-royal">Annapolis Royal</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/port-royal-acadia.jpg" alt="Port-Royal (Acadia)" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: attributed to Jean de Labat · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PortRoyalAcadia1702.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
